Z||000007||Jay||06-28-2001||09:55 PM||||How about adding a brake lock up that uses fluid rather than a cable?  I lost my e-brake when I changed to Cadillac drive train.  It could be attatched to the fronts rather than the rear and you could do burn outs at the track.  Anyone look into this?<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||acehilton||06-28-2001||10:09 PM||||I believe you must have a seperate operable mechanical (i.e. cable) emergency brake to be legal in most states. The reasoning behind this, I was told, was to allow for an alternate means of braking after a problem with the hydraulic brakes. <P>I know Colorado is that way, though we do not have an inspection program, so usually know one is the wiser. <P>||||reg||1
